{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/686223-what-other-resources-are-there","id":686223,"title":"What other resources are there?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-02T15:56:01-07:00","id":686223,"title":"What other resources are there?","content":"Are there any resources for learning the basics of play? I mean I have the book but, its kinda dense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8152-xizzicks","name":"Xizzicks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T17:27:25-07:00","id":686286,"title":"","content":"You could try watching or reading Actual Plays - recordings or transcripts of people playing RPGs - to get an idea of what a typical session looks like for other groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T17:33:23-07:00","id":686299,"title":"","content":"We exist! Ask whatever questions you need to here, we'll help you solve problems and listen as you sound stuff out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T18:15:21-07:00","id":686312,"title":"","content":"Thanks so much! Where do you get willpower? How do you get points for acquiring equipment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8152-xizzicks","name":"Xizzicks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T18:54:58-07:00","id":686320,"title":"","content":"Replenishing your willpower occurs through your anchors, which are your Mask, Dirge, and Touchstones. Basically, when you perform actions that reinforce your Mask, indulge your Dirge, or have a significant interaction with your Touchstone, you can restore one point or all of your willpower. How much you get back depends on the severity of your actions and a little bit of Storyteller fiat.<br /> <br /> \u200bPoints for acquiring equipment, if I'm reading your question correctly, are actually dots in resources that you can actually purchase at character creation or through experience in gameplay. Basically, if you have the same number of dots in resources as a piece of equipment has next to it, you can acquire the equipment reasonably. If a piece of equipment has more dots than you have in resources, then you'll either have to save up or team up with another character to get it.<br /> <br /> Hope this helped. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T20:06:26-07:00","id":686391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xizzicks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/686223-what-other-resources-are-there?p=686312#post686312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks so much! Where do you get willpower? How do you get points for acquiring equipment?</div> </div> </div> </div>This varies a little bit depending on if you're playing 1st edition or 2nd edition. I'm going to answer assuming 2nd edition, but please correct me if I'm wrong.<br /> <br /> There are a few ways to restore Willpower, which vary by character template. Mortal characters (and ghouls) automatically regain one point of Willpower every night when they sleep, and can also regain a point of Willpower by indulging in their Vice, which restores one Willpower once per scene at the most, or by acting in accordance with their Virtue, which restores all Willpower up to twice per game session.<br /> <br /> Vampire characters do not regain Willpower by resting, but can regain Willpower through their Masque and Dirge, similar to how Mortals do through their Virtue and Vice. Overcoming a minor obstacle in defense of your Mask or Dirge restores one point of Willpower, and facing significant setbacks in defense of either restores all Willpower. Vampires also have Touchstones, people who they interact with to keep themselves from completely losing touch with the human experience, and having a meaningful interaction with your Touchstone restores one point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> As for acquiring equipment, you do so with certain Merits - primarily the Resources Merit, but other Merits may be appropriate with Storyteller approval. The Resources Merit allows you to make purchase an item with an Availability rating equal to or one lower than your dots in the Merit up to once per game session, and any number of items with an Availability rating two or more dots lower than your dots in the Merit (within reason, the Storyteller has final say on how much is too much. You can also purchase an item with an Availability rating one higher than your dots in the Merit, but doing so reduces your effective Resources dots by one for a month of in-game time.<br /> <br /> Other Merits may be used to acquire equipment as well. That sort of thing is basically just up to Storyteller fiat. Personally, I allow most social Merits to work just like Resources, but only for purchases that would make sense to acquire with that Merit. For example, Status (Police) might be able to get you guns, but it won't get you Housing. Allies (Drug Dealers) might be able to get you Contraband, but it won't get you Fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T20:44:50-07:00","id":686438,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the advice! So it sounds like I could do this (Acording to my understanding of the rules thus far.) Write a few main characters representing all main covenants. Email my players as a character and inform them of a lead on a powerful artifact. Explain in person out of character to respond in terms of a few basic actions you explain to them such as, Investigating certain objects around them or asking characters about their covenant. etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8152-xizzicks","name":"Xizzicks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}